FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS — BUILD EXACTLY THIS

Construct a Utility Music/Media Player with the following precise feature set:

Core Controls (UI Buttons):
⏮ Previous Button — Navigates to the previous track in the playlist queue
▶ / ⏸ Play / Pause Toggle Button — Plays or pauses the currently loaded YouTube video
⏭ Next Button — Navigates to the next track in the playlist queue
🔊 Volume Control — A sleek slider input that controls playback volume in real time (range: 0–100), with a mute toggle icon that changes state visually

Playlist / URL Management:
A URL input field where the user can paste any valid YouTube video URL (standard https://www.youtube.com/watch?v= format and https://youtu.be/ short format must both be supported)
An "Add to Queue" button that parses the YouTube video ID from the URL and appends it to an internal playlist array
The playlist is displayed as a scrollable list below the player showing track number and video ID or title if retrievable
Clicking any item in the playlist loads and plays that track immediately
The player auto-advances to the next track when the current one ends

YouTube Playback Engine:
Use the YouTube IFrame Player API (https://www.youtube.com/iframe_api) loaded dynamically via script injection
The YouTube iframe is hidden visually (the player is audio/utility focused — the video renders but is visually minimized or hidden behind the UI) OR optionally shown in a clean thumbnail area — your architectural judgment applies here for best UX
Implement full YT.Player instantiation with onReady and onStateChange event handlers
Handle YT.PlayerState.ENDED to trigger auto-next behavior
Extract video ID correctly from both URL formats using a robust regex parser

UI/UX DESIGN REQUIREMENTS

Mobile-first** design — the player must look and function flawlessly on screens as small as 320px wide
Dark theme** with a premium feel — use a dark background (#0f0f0f or similar), with accent colors in a cool blue or violet palette (#6C63FF or similar), white text, and subtle glassmorphism or neumorphic styling on the card container
The player card must be centered on the page, max-width of 420px, with rounded corners, soft box shadows, and adequate padding
All buttons must have hover states, active press states, and smooth CSS transitions
Buttons should use SVG icons or Unicode symbols — no external icon libraries
The volume slider must be custom styled (no default browser appearance) — use CSS appearance: none with a styled thumb and track
The currently playing track should be highlighted in the playlist
A track title display area at the top of the player card (shows video ID or a placeholder like "Now Playing..." if no track is loaded)
Full responsive layout using Flexbox — no Grid required unless you determine it superior for a specific section

TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE REQUIREMENTS

Single .html file** — all CSS is in a ` block in , all JavaScript is in a  block before `
No external CSS frameworks** (no Bootstrap, no Tailwind CDN) — pure hand-written CSS only
No JavaScript frameworks** (no React, Vue, jQuery) — pure vanilla ES6+ JavaScript only
